From 21aba8daf4e4a21d1ee9d51f32c170bda3549f4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:31:29 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] kcm_samba: one list with two noun sections (User-Created
 Shares, Remote Share Mounts) instead of two side-by-side lists; models load
 after the first frame

Page type: List (docs/page-design.md 1, 4): KCM.ScrollViewKCM with one ListView; section headers are
Kirigami.ListSectionHeader, empty states are Kirigami.PlaceholderMessage (icon + sentence), View colours like the
information pages. The share rows (Path, Shared at, "Open folder properties..." button) and the mounted-share rows
(click opens the mount) are the same delegates; no label changed (ia aliases not needed). Rows kept with markers:
kcm_samba/UserShares, RemoteMounts, OpenProperties; inventory_check --kcm kcm_samba --strict: 0 lost.
Why: two 50 % wide lists with their own frames broke on narrow windows and looked unlike every other page (HIG-001,
design 2). The second list is the ListView footer (a Repeater over the mount model).

Also: ShareListItem called showPropertiesDialog through the id "view" of the page file; it now goes through its own
ListView.view, so it does not depend on ids of another file.

Speed (cause found in code): KSambaShareModel's constructor called reloadData() directly (invokeMethod on the same thread
is a direct call), which calls KSambaShare::instance() (reads the Samba config and user shares) and starts the Avahi
D-Bus query; SmbMountModel did Solid::Device::listFromType the same way. Both are now Qt::QueuedConnection, so the page
appears first and the rows are filled in from the event loop. After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Not built yet. Uncertain: the header/footer ColumnLayouts get height = implicitHeight (a layout in a ListView header has no
height otherwise); Repeater delegates keep using the injected ROLE_ names (no required properties, on purpose).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
